Engine-data round (DCS Control, 2026-11-25): [ofxr] dcs_motion_occlusion_fill (with dcs_motion, NVIDIA; default 0).
Around a moving object the background at the synthetic's instant is often seen in one real frame only: behind it the
object hid it in the previous frame, ahead of it the object hides it in the current one. Both endpoints of any vector
then disagree, 0036's colour checks fall back to the flow, and the flow (which matches both frames too) smears the
object's edge into a halo. Every DCS frame carries a class atlas beside its MVs, and the pair's previous frame's says
what that frame showed: dcs_motion_previous.hlsl (after the resample, one thread per cell, its own descriptor block
kDcsMotionFillBlock) maps each cell of the current field into the previous camera and keeps that frame's class rank
(sky 0, other G-buffer surfaces 1, models 2) in the field's flags above the resample's bits (w += 8 * (rank + 1)); the
composition (frame_synthesis.hlsl dcs_motion_occlusion_fill, UseGameMotion bit 12, called at the end of
dcs_motion_pixel only where the MVs' own weight is below 1) takes the farthest surface's vector within a cell, and
where its endpoint in one frame shows a nearer surface (the current frame's field; the previous frame's rank) and in
the other one does not, the other frame's sample alone. Not where the pixel at the instant is the nearer surface, nor
where the frames agree at the pixel or at the sample (still content over the world: a HUD). The previous frame's copy
is waited for where its mask was not bound. Without the key everything is as before (the existing XRFG_TEST_DCS_MOTION
scenes give the same numbers). tests/fg_engine_data.inc adds the fill to every case and checks it; at 640 x 480, MVs at
the periphery's texel (10 px), by day: behind a model 17.4 -> 5.8 sRGB mae, ahead 12.0 -> 8.4, a model and its 4 px
13.7 (flow) / 6.9 (MVs) -> 5.6, all 1.44 -> 1.36; at night behind 3.8 -> 2.8, all 0.42 -> 0.40; HUD, smoke and
particles unchanged within 0.3; at 2560 x 1920 behind 14.5 -> 3.3, all 0.70 -> 0.59. Cost (XRFG_TEST_FG_ENGINE_DATA_BENCH,
5424 x 5356, both eyes, RTX 5090): composition 1157 -> 1214 us median per pair; no new resource (one descriptor block per
work slot).
Touched functions (for merges): D3D12FrameSynthesizer::Impl members (dcs_motion_feature_bits, dcs_motion_previous_pipeline,
pair_previous_class_read), create_root_signature_and_pipelines (the pass's pipeline), create_dcs_motion_resources (one
line), record_dcs_motion (one OR into pair_motion_bits), record_nvidia_pair (one call after record_dcs_motion),
create_work_slots (the heap's size), submit_pair (the previous frame's fence wait), new record_dcs_motion_previous_class;
frame_synthesis.hlsl: new dcs_motion_depth_rank / dcs_motion_current_cell / dcs_motion_previous_rank /
dcs_motion_occlusion_fill, one block at the end of dcs_motion_pixel.
